  "tests": "TS2 tests are byte-identical copies of the source tests: shared JS/Rust vector parity (order ids, signing messages, signatures, request_sha256), TS2 key files (V4 refused by name), installation pins and the client against a synthetic TS2 server. The source-closed schema6 suites test_agent.py and test_context.py are copied with package-local vector paths. The fixtures are byte-identical to verifiable-testnet/trade-settlement/fixtures and onboarding/web.",
  "kit_extensions": "fairvenue_mcp/ and tests/test_mcp_server.py are the agent kit's optional MCP server (the pyproject mcp extra), not imported protocol source. They only call the public fairvenue_schema6 API and never change the byte-identical files above. Since TS2 the whole fairvenue_schema6 package, including installation.py and the deployment pins, is imported unchanged."
